  "title": "Knowledge Graphs",
  "content": "# Knowledge Graph Systems\n\nKnowledge graphs represent information as interconnected entities (nodes) and \nrelationships (edges). They power search engines (Google Knowledge Graph), \nrecommendation systems, and question-answering pipelines.\n\n## Key Concepts\n- **Nodes**: Entities (people, places, concepts)\n- **Edges**: Relationships between entities\n- **Properties**: Attributes attached to nodes or edges\n\n## Applications in Personal Knowledge Management\n- Auto-linking related notes via semantic similarity\n- Visualizing idea clusters and knowledge gaps\n- Enabling graph-based search and traversal\n\nForce-directed graph layouts (like Cytoscape.js's COSE algorithm) use \nphysics simulation to position nodes — connected nodes attract, while \nunconnected nodes repel, creating natural visual clusters.",
  "para_category": "resources",
